{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"SimpleX.SimpleX-Chat","latestVersion":"7.0.3","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"SimpleX - the first messaging network operating without user identifiers of any kind - 100% private by design! iOS,\nAndroid and desktop apps 📱!","license":"AGPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/simplex-chat/simplex-chat/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"SimpleX - the first messaging network operating without user identifiers of any kind - 100% private by design! iOS,\nAndroid and desktop apps 📱!","license":"AGPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/simplex-chat/simplex-chat/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Unlike any other existing messaging platform, SimpleX has no identifiers assigned to the users - it does not use phone\nnumbers (like Signal or WhatsApp), domain-based addresses (like email, XMPP or Matrix), usernames (like Telegram),\npublic keys or even random numbers (like all other messengers) to identify its users - we do not even know how many\npeople use SimpleX.","moniker":"simplex","name":"SimpleX Chat","packageUrl":"https://simplex.chat/","publisher":"SimpleX","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/simplex-chat","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/simplex-chat/simplex-chat/releases/tag/v7.0.3","tags":["chat","double-ratchet","e2ee","encryption","haskell","messaging","privacy","protocol","security"]}},"longDescription":"Unlike any other existing messaging platform, SimpleX has no identifiers assigned to the users - it does not use phone\nnumbers (like Signal or WhatsApp), domain-based addresses (like email, XMPP or Matrix), usernames (like Telegram),\npublic keys or even random numbers (like all other messengers) to identify its users - we do not even know how many\npeople use SimpleX.","moniker":"simplex","name":"SimpleX Chat","packageUrl":"https://simplex.chat/","publisher":"SimpleX","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/simplex-chat","releaseNotesU